# liquid-snipe — PROJECT

## Objective

"Build a Solana liquidity-sniping bot in Rust."
"Listen to first-liquidity events on major Solana DEXes / launchpads, filter through one operator-configured strategy, execute WSOL-denominated buys against the originating DEX, and manage each position event-driven through a list of sell triggers — within a written risk profile."

"Clean-room implementation in a new Rust crate sibling to the existing `liquid-snipe/` POC directory. The POC's research findings — entry/exit signal taxonomy, the price-from-tx insight, the strategy profiles — inform the design but are NOT the code we're shipping. No file from `liquid-snipe/` is read by the new bot at runtime."

"Directory: `liquid-snipe-rs/` (sibling to `liquid-snipe/`)."
"Workspace binary: `liquid-snipe`. Crates: `liquid-snipe`, `liquid-snipe-core`, `liquid-snipe-stream`, `liquid-snipe-strategy`, `liquid-snipe-simulator`, `liquid-snipe-exec`."

## Scope

Scope {
  // DEXes sol-trade-sdk can execute against
  in = ["pump.fun", "PumpSwap", "Raydium AMM v4", "Raydium CPMM", "Meteora DAMM v2"]

  // Signal evaluation runs but no buy/sell tx
  capture_only = ["Raydium CLMM", "Meteora DLMM", "Orca Whirlpool"]

  // WSOL-only quote: universal pair on fresh pools.
  // Dropping USDC/USDT removes edge cases (different ATAs, different SOL→USDC paths).
  quote = "WSOL"

  // SOL↔WSOL wrap helper in-scope so operator can top up WSOL ATA from native SOL without a separate tool.
  helpers = ["wrap-sol"]

  out = ["Jupiter aggregator routing", "cross-DEX arb", "multi-wallet", "web UI", "in-app wallet generation"]
  wallet = "operator-provided"
}

## Strategy model

"One configurable Strategy = one BuyTrigger + ordered SellTriggers + one RiskProfile."
"Operator swaps or tunes any of them via config. Bot loads exactly one strategy at boot."

### BuyTrigger

"AND-combined filters on a captured chain event (CREATE / INIT / MIGRATE / DEPOSIT). All must pass."

interface BuyTrigger {
  event_kinds                        // default ["INIT", "MIGRATE"]
  min_sol_liquidity                  // event solValue ≥ N
  dex_allowlist                      // subset of capture-DEXes
  dex_blocklist
  quote_mints                        // default ["WSOL"]
  require_renounced_authorities      // mint + freeze authority both null
  require_lp_burned                  // ≥95% of LP token at burn / locker
  max_top10_holder_concentration     // top-10 hold ≤ X fraction of supply
  min_holder_count                   // total token holders ≥ N
  max_market_cap_sol                 // supply × spot price ≤ N
  deployer_max_prior_launches        // prior tokens by signer ≤ N (serial-rugger proxy)
  deployer_blocklist_path            // hard-deny JSON file, hot-reloadable
  enrichment_timeout_ms              // wait for async mint enrichment before reject
}

constraints {
  "RPC-derived filters (renounced authorities, LP burn, holder concentration, deployer history) are computed by the enrichment task and read from cache on the hot path."
  "A strategy that requires an enrichment field rejects the candidate if the cache is cold past enrichment_timeout_ms — the same mint gets a warm cache for the next event."
}

### SellTriggers

"OR-combined, evaluated in priority order on every chain event for the position's mint. The bot ships seven trigger kinds; operator composes any subset."

interface SellTrigger {
  // kind is one of:
  hard_stop         // params: stop_pct (negative). Exit fully when return ≤ stop_pct.
  ladder            // params: rungs [{profit, sell}]. Sell `sell` fraction at each profit rung.
  trailing_stop     // params: trail_pct. Exit fully when drop from peak ≥ trail_pct, only after entry is in profit.
  liquidity_drain   // params: drain_pct. Exit when pool quote reserve < drain_pct × baseline.
  decay             // params: samples_n. Exit on N consecutive non-positive returns.
  insider_sell      // params: insider_pct. Exit when any address in the position's insider set sells ≥ insider_pct of supply in one tx. See SPEC §4.4 for set construction.
  time_stop         // params: hold_sec. Exit after holding for hold_sec.
}

SellPriority {
  // When multiple fire on the same event, this is the order (highest first):
  order = ["hard_stop", "ladder", "trailing_stop", "liquidity_drain", "insider_sell", "decay", "time_stop"]

  "time_stop and decay also run on a wall-clock heartbeat (default 100ms) for the case where nobody else is trading the mint."
}

### RiskProfile

"Bankroll-relative, not absolute."

interface RiskProfile {
  bankroll_sol              // auto-detected from wallet balance on boot, refreshed on every fill
  max_total_risk_pct = 50   // halt new entries while open exposure > X% of bankroll
  max_per_trade_risk_pct = 5
  max_daily_loss_pct = 10   // halt new entries when today's realised PnL ≤ -X%
  max_open_positions = 4
  min_wallet_sol_floor = 0.05  // absolute SOL
  default_slippage_bps      // starting; adapted by slippage controller
}

## Requirements

Functional {
  R1_LiveEventStream {
    "One Yellowstone gRPC subscription delivers every entry candidate and every price/exit update on every open position."
    "Endpoint and auth are config-driven."
    "Helius WS logsNotifications is the fallback when gRPC is unavailable."
    "Both are hot-swappable (see R6)."
  }

  R2_SingleStrategy {
    "Boot loads one Strategy (BuyTrigger + SellTriggers + RiskProfile) from config."
    "No code change required to retune."
  }

  R3_BuyExecution {
    "When BuyTrigger fires AND RiskProfile approves: build TradeBuyParams via sol-trade-sdk, sign with configured wallet, submit through SWQOS."
    "Tx submission runs in a spawned task — hot loop never blocks."
    "Buy failure marks the position `failed` immediately. No auto-retry on the same opportunity (sniping is time-sensitive; missed entry is gone)."
  }

  R4_AdaptiveSlippage {
    "Slippage controller tracks consecutive buy failures across a rolling window."
    "After N consecutive failures (default 5), increase global slippage by slippage_bump_bps (default +1000 bps = +10%) up to max_slippage_bps cap."
    "After a success or decay window expires: reset."
  }

  R5_PositionMgmt {
    "Each open position is updated on every chain event for its mint, delivered by the same gRPC subscription."
    "No position polling. Wall-clock heartbeat (default 100ms) covers time/decay safety nets only."
  }

  R6_HotReload {
    "All endpoints, wallet path, strategy, risk profile, SWQOS providers, gas, and tuning live in one TOML."
    "SIGHUP triggers a config reload: swap gRPC endpoint, SWQOS providers, adaptive-slippage params without restart."
    "Strategy / RiskProfile changes also reload but apply only to NEW positions; in-flight positions keep their original triggers."
  }

  R7_RiskEnforcement {
    "Before every new entry, the risk engine checks total open exposure, per-trade size, daily loss, open-position count, wallet floor."
    "Any violation rejects the candidate with reason logged to signal_decisions."
  }

  R8_WalletFromConfig {
    "Wallet keypair is loaded from a config-specified path or environment variable."
    "The bot NEVER creates a wallet."
    "Missing/invalid wallet is a fatal boot error in `live` mode (warning in `paper`)."
  }

  R9_Modes {
    "Three modes selectable via CLI flag (priority) or config (fallback)."
    live    = "real on-chain buys/sells via SWQOS. Default if neither CLI nor config specifies."
    paper   = "full pipeline + simulator-based fills, written to DuckDB with tx_signature = paper_<uuid>."
    observe = "capture + signal evaluation only, no buys."
  }

  R10_Persistence {
    "DuckDB at data/liquid-snipe.duckdb holds chain_events, signal_decisions, mint_enrichment cache, positions (append-only), fills, blocklist."
    "Hot loop never writes directly — a persistence task batches writes (default every 1s or 1024 rows)."
  }

  R11_ModularSWQOS {
    "The [[swqos]] config array configures any combination of providers sol-trade-sdk supports: default RPC, Jito, Temporal/Nozomi, ZeroSlot, FlashBlock, BlockRazor, Astralane, NextBlock, SpeedLanding."
    "Each entry takes API key + region OR custom URL (Temporal self-hosted = own relay)."
    "Concurrent multi-provider sends use the SDK parallel-submit path; fastest wins."
  }

  R12_Stats {
    "`liquid-snipe stats [--window 24h]` summarises: open positions, realised PnL by day, hit rate, mean / median / max / drawdown, exit-reason histogram, slippage controller state, kill-switch state."
    "Plain text + a `--json` flag for piping."
  }
}

NonFunctional {
  N1_Latency {
    hot_loop_frame_p99   = "< 500µs"     // gRPC update → decide → spawn submit
    buy_submit_p50       = "< 250ms"     // spawn → confirmed by SWQOS
    buy_submit_p99       = "< 1s"        // on dedicated gRPC + colocated SWQOS
    sell_submit_p99      = "< 1s"
  }

  N2_Reliability {
    "All upstreams (gRPC, WS, RPC) auto-reconnect with exponential backoff capped at 5s."
    "Pipeline never aborts on a single upstream failure."
    "SWQOS provider failures are isolated — one dead provider doesn't take down the rest."
  }

  N3_Observability {
    "Structured JSON logs (tracing) per chain event, per signal decision, per submitted tx, per fill, per slippage adjustment, per kill-switch trip."
    "Per-frame timing histogram exported."
  }

  N4_Footprint {
    "Single binary. DuckDB file under data/."
    "No external services beyond RPC + gRPC + SWQOS (all third-party)."
  }
}

## Acceptance criteria

Acceptance {
  AC1_BootDryObserve {
    cmd = "liquid-snipe --config config.toml --observe"
    "Connects within 5s."
    "Writes chain events to DuckDB chain_events for ≥3 distinct DEXes inside 60s of capture during normal mainnet activity."
    "Emits one signal_decisions row per (event, strategy) including rejections with structured reasons."
  }

  AC2_FrameBudget {
    "Regression test replays 10_000 recorded gRPC updates through the hot loop with all background tasks stubbed."
    target_p99   = "< 500µs"
    target_p99_9 = "< 1ms"
    "CI gate."
  }

  AC3_PaperE2E {
    cmd = "liquid-snipe --config config.toml --paper"
    duration = "60 minutes against live gRPC"
    "BuyTrigger fires at least once with operator-tuned threshold."
    "Complete simulated trade (entry + ≥1 sell) recorded in positions and fills."
    "`liquid-snipe stats` reports the result."
  }

  AC4_LiveBuyReal {
    cmd = "liquid-snipe --config config.toml --live"
    setup = "funded test wallet, max_per_trade_risk_pct = 1"
    "One BuyTrigger fires; real buy lands on-chain (confirmed) within N1 latency budget."
    "Position is exited (any reason) with a real on-chain sell."
    "Realised PnL row written to positions with actual on-chain prices."
    "`liquid-snipe replay <tx_signature>` prints the full decision and execution trail."
  }

  AC5_RiskKillSwitch {
    setup = "max_daily_loss_pct = 10, bankroll_sol = 1.0"
    "Manually insert a synthetic -0.15 SOL realised loss row (15% of bankroll)."
    "Next entry candidate rejected with reason `risk:daily-loss-exceeded`, persisted to signal_decisions, visible in stats."
  }

  AC6_HotReload {
    "Edit TOML: change gRPC endpoint AND one SellTrigger threshold. SIGHUP."
    "gRPC reconnects to new endpoint within 5s without restart."
    "New positions opened after SIGHUP use the updated SellTrigger."
    "In-flight positions continue with their original triggers (logged at info)."
  }

  AC7_AdaptiveSlippage {
    "Force 5 consecutive simulated buy failures (config: stub a SWQOS that always errors)."
    "Global slippage was bumped by exactly slippage_bump_bps."
    "A successful buy resets the failure counter."
    "Slippage never exceeds max_slippage_bps."
  }
}

## Risks and unknowns

Risks {
  InfraLatency {
    "Yellowstone gRPC tier and SWQOS provider latency dominate N1."
    "The bot frame budget is internal; end-to-end number bounded by operator's plan."
  }

  StrategyExpectancy {
    "POC suggested positive expectancy on whale-filtered events but n is small."
    "Live paper-mode runs are how expectancy gets measured."
  }

  ProcessedRollback {
    "Hot loop acts on Processed events (~400ms ahead of Confirmed)."
    "Small fraction of events get reverted; a position acted on a reverted entry tx must be force-closed at market."
    "SPEC documents the recovery path."
  }

  DexCoverageGap {
    "CLMM / DLMM / Whirlpool are capture-only in v1."
    "If the strongest signals start showing up there, plan a v2 Jupiter routing path."
  }

  ReservePoisoning {
    "Deployer can drain a pool while our partial sell is mid-flight."
    mitigation = "Never cancel an in-flight tx; preempt with a higher fee on the next tx (SPEC §4.3)."
  }
}

## Open decisions

OpenDecisions {
  GrpcEndpointProvider {
    options = ["Helius dedicated (Developer+)", "Triton", "Jito Shredstream", "self-hosted Yellowstone"]
    "Decision affects monthly cost AND N1 latency ceiling."
    "Provider research happening in a separate session."
    "SPEC carries a literal placeholder endpoint until resolved."
  }

  SWQOSDayOne {
    "Default-RPC ships out of the box. Under that config, live mode will NOT hit N1 (p99 < 1s)."
    "Adding Jito / Temporal / ZeroSlot / etc needs API keys and a per-provider tip budget."
    "Operator picks; bot supports any subset."
  }
}

